  "operative_text": "Sec 2 short title: Sections 2 to 7, inclusive, of this act may be cited as\nSec 3 findings and declarations: The Legislature representing the People of the State\nSec 4 definitions: As used in sections 2 to 7, inclusive, of this act unless\nSec 5 background check on private sale: an unlicensed person shall not sell or transfer a firearm to another unlicensed person unless a licensed dealer first conducts a background check on the buyer or transferee in compliance with this section.\nSec 6 exemptions: The provisions of section 5 of this act do not apply to:\nSec 7 penalty: For a first offense involving the sale or transfer of one or more firearms, is guilty of a gross misdemeanor;\nSec 8 amends NRS 179A.140 (no fee for checks): An agency of criminal justice shall not charge a fee for providing such information to another agency of criminal justice\nSec 9 repeals the 2016 initiative provisions: NRS 202.2531, 202.2533, 202.2535, 202.254, 202.2541 and 202.2543 are hereby repealed.\nSec 10 effective date: This act becomes effective on January 2, 2020.\nSummary of rule as read to the Senate: a person who does not hold a license as a firearm dealer, importer or manufacturer cannot sell or transfer a firearm to another unlicensed person unless a licensed dealer first conducts a background check on the buyer or transferee.",
